# Every text file is checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with git's default core.autocrlf rewrites
# LF to CRLF, and three tests that compare checked-in fixture bytes against
# what the code regenerates fail on every GitHub Windows cell while passing
# on the local VM, whose tree arrives as a tarball and is never rewritten
# (2026-09-05, ci-extended run 33969574449: firewall_ladder_proof's
# ratio_table_recomputed_from_reduce_is_byte_identical and
# checked_in_corpus_matches_the_seeded_generator, subscription_pressure's
# the_policy_does_not_invent_task_completion). The token estimates in the
# ratio table differed too -- CRLF is more bytes -- so "byte-identical" was
# the honest name for what broke.
#
# The Windows batch and PowerShell scripts under scripts/dev/windows/ already
# run with LF from that tarball, so no exception is carved out for them.
* text=auto eol=lf
